  "sections": {
    "BASICS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "An acute to subacute contagious viral disease with an almost exclusive respiratory manifestation caused by influenza viruses.",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Canine influenza viruses (CIV) are influenza type A viruses that developed from equine (H3N8, USA) or avian (H3N2; East Asia) influenza viruses. Although the viruses originated in other species, the H3 viruses are considered “canine influenza viruses” as they are now transmissible dog to dog. Influenza H7N2 is an avian influenza A virus that was documented in shelter cats. H1N1 human pandemic influenza is also capable of infecting dogs and cats, but there is no evidence of transmission.",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Natural route of infection is airborne particles or oral contact with contaminated surfaces. Replication of the virus appears to be restricted to epithelial cells of the upper and lower airways, with possible involvement of alveolar macrophages. Antibody response detectable by 8 days post infection and titers",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "immune responses have not been defined.",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "H3N8 CIV activity was first detected in",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "racing greyhounds in the United States in",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "2004 and has subsequently been identified in",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "dogs across the country.",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "H3N2 CIV was detected in South Korea in",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "2007, but existed in China several years earlier;",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "genetic lineage is of avian origin and probably",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "arose in East Asia.",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "H3N2 CIV infection causes more severe",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "clinical signs, is more easily transmissible, and",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "is shed for a longer period than H3N8 CIV.",
              "pdf_page": 855,
              "printed_page": 773,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "remain detectable for>1 year. Protective"
            }
          ]
        },
